"""Render non-preprocessor frontend timings and evidence-backed priorities."""
import json
import pathlib

ROOT = pathlib.Path('suite/reports')
p = json.loads((ROOT / 'c-frontend-stages-20261015.json').read_text())
a = json.loads((ROOT / 'c-frontend-stages-analysis-20261015.json').read_text())
data = {'summaries': p['summaries'], 'workloads': a['workloads'],
        'stacks': {k: {'category_percent': v['category_percent'], 'attribution': v['attribution']} for k, v in a['stacks'].items()}}
page = r'''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:transparent;color:var(--foreground,#25252c);font:14px/1.5 var(--font-sans,system-ui)}h2{font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-.4px;margin:0 0 6px}h3{font-size:16px;margin:22px 0 10px}p{margin:5px 0 12px}.muted,small{color:var(--muted-foreground,#777)}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:16px 0}button,select{font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border,#ddd);border-radius:7px;padding:6px 10px;background:transparent;color:inherit;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--accent-surface,#eeefff);border-color:var(--accent,#7181de)}.legend{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:12px;margin:10px 0 14px}.legend span:before{content:'';display:inline-block;width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--c);margin-right:5px}.row{margin:13px 0}.label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:4px}.track{height:23px;display:flex;background:var(--muted,#eee);overflow:hidden;border-radius:4px}.seg{height:100%}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}th,td{text-align:right;padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#ddd)}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left;padding-left:0}thead th{color:var(--muted-foreground,#777);font-weight:500}.table{overflow-x:auto}.finding{padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border,#ddd)}.finding p{margin:3px 0 0}.metric{color:var(--accent,#7181de);font-weight:600}.foot{font-size:11px;margin-top:20px}.columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}@media(max-width:540px){.columns{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}h2{font-size:20px}table{font-size:11px}th,td{padding:7px 3px}}
</style></head><body><h2>Beyond preprocessing: C frontend profile</h2><p class="muted">44 files · 1.99 million tokens · 6,136 functions · commit 2808137</p><p>Lexing and parsing lead on Lua and QuickJS. SQLite spends the largest share in IR generation. All three offer substantial work beyond preprocessing.</p><div class="controls"><select id="mode" aria-label="Compilation mode"><option value="normal">Normal mode</option><option value="debug">Debug-info mode</option></select><button id="ms" aria-pressed="true">Milliseconds</button><button id="share" aria-pressed="false">Stage share</button></div><div class="legend" id="legend"></div><div id="chart"></div><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Compile API</th><th>Lex</th><th>Parse / types</th><th>IR gen</th><th>Cleanup</th></tr></thead><tbody id="times"></tbody></table></div><small>Milliseconds per whole application. Bars sum stage medians; the compile-API column is measured separately. Returned module destruction is excluded.</small><h3>Where I would look for gains</h3><div class="finding"><strong>1. Replace the lexer's linear punctuation search.</strong><p><span class="metric">9.9–16.6% of all frontend samples</span> sit in comparisons at this one callsite. Release assembly confirms a 48-entry prefix-search loop calling memcmp. Dispatch on the leading byte and test only valid longer spellings. This is the clearest first experiment.</p></div><div class="finding"><strong>2. Reduce parser token and string cloning.</strong><p>String cloning under parsing accounts for <span class="metric">3.2–6.8% of all samples</span>; allocator work under parsing adds overlapping cost. Parser::eat calls advance, which clones the token, then discards it. Start with a position-only consume path; consider identifier storage changes after measuring that.</p></div><div class="finding"><strong>3. Investigate SSA predecessor discovery.</strong><p><span class="metric">16.8% of SQLite samples</span> are under seal_block; the SSA builder as a whole is 26.9%. find_preds scans every built block each time a block is sealed. Maintaining predecessor edges could remove repeated graph scans, but this is a larger correctness-sensitive change. The profile does not isolate the inlined scan from parameter work.</p></div><div class="columns"><section><h3>Largest translation units</h3><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Frontend</th><th>IR gen</th></tr></thead><tbody id="files"></tbody></table><small>Normal-mode medians; large functions and control-flow graphs are useful stress cases.</small></section><section><h3>Other measured costs</h3><p>Parser/token/AST cleanup is about <strong>4–6%</strong> of stage time. Total allocator activity is <strong>18–22%</strong> of stack samples, spread across lexing, parsing, IR generation, and destruction.</p><p class="muted">Allocator and clone samples overlap. Debug-info mode changes local-variable storage and SSA work, so lower IR-generation time there is not a speedup for identical output.</p></section></div><p class="foot">Method: nine serial warm resident-input rounds in both modes; baseline and staged APIs shuffled, source order rotated. All 44 input hashes match the original corpus. Every process verifies IR and exact Debug IR equality between staged and public APIs before timing. Staged/baseline median ratios range 0.983–1.003. Four separate six-second stack captures cover all three normal workloads and SQLite debug. Samples include returned-module destruction; timed stage boundaries exclude it. Optimized inlining limits attribution. Preprocessing, optimizer, backend, filesystem reads, verification, startup and warmup are excluded from stage timing. Candidate gains above are hypotheses, not measured speedups.</p><script>
const D=__DATA__;const apps=['lua','quickjs','sqlite'],labels={lua:'Lua',quickjs:'QuickJS',sqlite:'SQLite'},keys=['lex_ms','parse_ms','irgen_ms','cleanup_ms'],names=['Lex','Parse / types','IR generation','Cleanup'],colors=['#4e9ad7','#40a890','#e7a04e','#9099a7'];let share=false;const mode=document.getElementById('mode');document.getElementById('ms').onclick=()=>{share=false;draw()};document.getElementById('share').onclick=()=>{share=true;draw()};mode.onchange=draw;document.getElementById('legend').innerHTML=names.map((n,i)=>'<span style="--c:'+colors[i]+'">'+n+'</span>').join('');function draw(){document.getElementById('ms').setAttribute('aria-pressed',!share);document.getElementById('share').setAttribute('aria-pressed',share);const entries=apps.map(app=>{const s=D.summaries[app+':'+mode.value],v=keys.map(k=>s.staged.median_ms[k]);return{app,s,v,total:v.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)}});const max=Math.max(...entries.map(e=>e.total));document.getElementById('chart').innerHTML=entries.map(e=>'<div class="row"><div class="label"><strong>'+labels[e.app]+'</strong><span>'+e.total.toFixed(1)+' ms</span></div><div class="track">'+e.v.map((v,i)=>'<div class="seg" style="background:'+colors[i]+';width:'+(100*v/(share?e.total:max))+'%" title="'+names[i]+': '+v.toFixed(1)+' ms · '+(100*v/e.total).toFixed(1)+'%"></div>').join('')+'</div></div>').join('');document.getElementById('times').innerHTML=entries.map(e=>'<tr><th>'+labels[e.app]+'</th><td><strong>'+e.s.baseline.median_ms.total_ms.toFixed(1)+'</strong></td>'+e.v.map(v=>'<td>'+v.toFixed(1)+'</td>').join('')+'</tr>').join('');document.getElementById('files').innerHTML=apps.map(app=>D.workloads[app].top_files[0]).map(f=>'<tr><th>'+f.name+'</th><td>'+f.total_ms.toFixed(1)+' ms</td><td>'+f.irgen_ms.toFixed(1)+' ms</td></tr>').join('')}draw();console.log('Loaded 44 inputs; six application/mode summaries; four stack captures.');
</script></body></html>'''
(ROOT / 'c-frontend-stages-20261015.html').write_text(page.replace('__DATA__', json.dumps(data, separators=(',', ':'))))
